{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And he shall bring it.</b> Even a single turtledove he may bring (Sifra)." "<b>The priest, and shall wring.</b> Melikhah is not done with an implement, but with the priest's fingernail itself — he cuts with his thumbnail opposite the nape and severs its neck until he reaches the signs and cuts them (ibid.)." "<b>And its blood shall be drained out.</b> Like מֵץ אַפַּיִם (Proverbs 30), כִּי אָפֵס הַמֵּץ (Isaiah 16) — he presses the place of slaughter against the wall of the altar, and the blood drains and runs down (Zevaḥim 65)." "<b>And shall wring, and burn, and be drained out.</b> Should you say: how so — since he burns, does he drain? Rather: just as the burning is the head by itself and the body by itself, so too the melikhah. And the plain sense of the verse is inverted — וּמָלַק וְהִקְטִיר, and before the burning, its blood has already been drained."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:43.098264279Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}